                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I am very grateful that Governor Healey has decided to pause the plans to close Pappas Rehabilitation Hospital for Children in Canton and to assemble a qualified team to make further assessments.\n\nI would like to thank the Pappas patients, families, and amazing staff as well as State Senators Paul Feeney, Mike Rush, and\u00a0Bill Driscoll,\u00a0and\u00a0State Representatives Bill Galvin, John Rogers, and Ted Philips, and the families of Canton for their tireless advocacy to keep the hospital open.\n\nThrough collaboration with the healthcare community and colleagues in government, I am hopeful that we will find a way to keep Pappas open permanently, so we can continue to provide the best possible support to the Commonwealth\u2019s most vulnerable children and their families.",
                "text_lang": "en",
