                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "I am proud to reintroduce the \u201cK2 Veterans Total Coverage Act\u201d with my colleague, @RepMarkGreen. \n\n\u00a0After more than five years of bipartisan investigation, there is now irrefutable evidence that American service members were exposed to cancer-causing hazards and other toxins while deployed at Karshi-Khanabad Air Base (K2) following the September 11th, 2001, terrorist attacks.\u00a0Yet there is still no assurance that the VA will accept their claims for service-connected disability benefits.\u00a0\n\nThis bipartisan bill will ensure that our K2 veterans are eligible for the benefits they have already earned for courageous services rendered to our Country.",
                "text_lang": "en",
